# Teodor, night foreman at the Freight Depot. docs/slice-spec.md §7.
# Voice: short, plain, subtext. People in a police state talk around things.
#
# Context you can test: aid_runs, knows_skim, lied, confessed, path, loyalty,
# legitimacy, heat, week. Setting `choice` tells the rules what you did:
# "honest", "blackmail", "lie", or "" (nothing decided).

== meet
> Container yard, two in the morning. The cranes are still. One man is not.
TEODOR: You're the one handing out soup in the dormitories.
YOU: Some of it.
TEODOR: Soup gets people killed here. Did they tell you that?
YOU: They told me you run the night shift.
TEODOR: I run cranes. Nights, I run cranes.
> He lights a cigarette with a hand that doesn't shake.
TEODOR: My brother ran a newsletter. Four pages. Recipes, mostly. Some opinions.
TEODOR: He's in Kell now. Six years. For recipes.
YOU: I'm sorry.
TEODOR: Everyone's sorry. Come back when you're something else.
-> END

== talk
> The tea shack behind Gate 4. Teodor pours two cups and drinks neither.
TEODOR: Back again.
if knows_skim -> talk_knows
-> talk_menu

== talk_knows
> He watches you watch the cargo manifests on the wall.
TEODOR: You've been listening in the depot. People notice who listens.
-> talk_menu

== talk_menu
* Tell him what you're really doing. -> honest
* [if knows_skim] You know about the cargo. -> blackmail
* I can get your brother out of Kell. -> lie
* Talk about nothing for an hour. -> around

== honest
set choice = "honest"
YOU: We want the yards back. Not burned. Back.
if aid_runs >= 2 -> honest_yes
TEODOR: Everyone wants something back.
TEODOR: Words are cheap at two in the morning. Show me, don't tell me.
> He means the depot. He means his people eating.
-> END

== honest_yes
> He turns the cup in his hands.
TEODOR: The flour came twice. Nobody got arrested for eating it.
TEODOR: That's more than the government managed.
TEODOR: All right. The night shift is with you. Don't make me sorry.
-> END

== blackmail
set choice = "blackmail"
YOU: Crates go out the east gate light. Smugglers pay you for the difference.
> He sets the cup down very carefully.
TEODOR: And who would you tell?
YOU: Nobody. If you help us.
TEODOR: So that's what you are.
TEODOR: Fine. I'll carry your boxes. Don't turn your back on me.
-> END

== lie
set choice = "lie"
YOU: We have people inside Kell. Help us, and your brother walks out.
> Something in his face opens. It is hard to watch.
TEODOR: You can do that?
YOU: We can do that.
TEODOR: Then I'm yours. The whole shift is yours.
> There is no one inside Kell. There never was.
-> END

== around
set choice = ""
> You talk about the weather, the price of bread, a football match neither of you watched.
TEODOR: Good tea. Come back when you've decided who you are.
-> END

== confess
> You find him on the crane ladder at shift change.
* Just say it. -> confess_plain
* Start with why you lied. -> confess_why
* Tell him what he's done for the cause first. -> confess_soft

== confess_plain
YOU: There's no one in Kell. There's no plan for your brother. I lied.
-> confess_wait

== confess_why
YOU: I needed the dock. I needed it fast. So I told you what you wanted to hear.
YOU: There's no plan for Kell.
-> confess_wait

== confess_soft
YOU: The strike, the shift, all of it. None of this happens without you.
YOU: And none of it was fair to you. There's no plan for Kell.
-> confess_wait

== confess_wait
> He doesn't answer. Below you, the cranes start up one by one.
-> END

== confess_stayed
> Three days of silence. Then he's at the safehouse door with a crate of parts.
TEODOR: My brother would have told me the truth sooner.
TEODOR: He'd also have stayed. So.
-> END

== confess_left
> His locker at the depot is empty. Someone has scratched out the name tape.
MARA: He said to tell you he's not angry. He said angry would mean he expected better.
-> END

== found_out
> A guard at Kell takes a carton of cigarettes to answer one question.
> Teodor learns there was never anyone inside. Not from you.
MARA: He came by the safehouse. Didn't knock. Just stood across the street.
MARA: Then he went back to the depot and told the night shift to go home.
-> END

== betrayal
> Sirens on Varga Street at four in the morning. They knew which door.
KESH: They came straight for the safehouse. Nobody followed us. Somebody told them.
KESH: Teodor was the only one who knew the new address.
> You remember what he said. Don't turn your back on me.
-> END

== strike
> The east dock, end of shift. Teodor stands on a cable drum.
TEODOR: They took my brother for four pages of recipes.
TEODOR: Tonight the cranes stop. Nobody loads anything for anybody until they listen.
> One by one, the floodlights go dark.
-> END
